sequenceDiagram
    %% OVIC EON — API Request Lifecycle and Reliability
    %% Document ID: EON-ARCH-DIAG-API-LIFE-001

    autonumber
    participant Client as Developer / Client
    participant API as FastAPI Request Handler
    participant RateLimiter as Rate Limiter (Token Bucket)
    participant Validator as Pydantic Schema Validator
    participant Service as Internal EON Core Service

    Client->>API: HTTP Request (POST /api/v1/config/reload)
    API->>API: Generate unique request_id (UUID4)
    API->>RateLimiter: Check client IP bucket (Max 60/min)
    alt Rate Limit Exceeded
        RateLimiter-->>API: Limit Exceeded
        API-->>Client: 429 Too Many Requests (Retry-After: 30)
    else Limit OK
        API->>Validator: Parse & validate request payload
        alt Validation Error
            Validator-->>API: ValidationError (Invalid JSON / Types)
            API-->>Client: 400 Bad Request (RFC 7807 with request_id)
        else Payload Valid
            API->>Service: Execute operation with timeout=2.0s
            alt Operation Succeeded
                Service-->>API: Return response data
                API-->>Client: 200 OK (Response JSON + Header: X-Request-ID)
            else Service Timeout / Degraded
                Service-->>API: TimeoutException
                API-->>Client: 503 Service Unavailable (Fallback Details)
            end
        end
    end
